The benchmark also offsets the Sun's velocity by the total momentum so momentum is zeroed:

```
offset_momentum: for each body, sun.vx -= body.vx * body.mass / solar_mass, etc.
```

Energy computation:

```
energy = sum over bodies of 0.5 * mass * (vx²+vy²+vz²)
        - sum over pairs i<j of mass_i * mass_j / distance(i,j)
```

The symplectic integration (velocity Verlet-ish as in the CLBG version):

```
for each step:
    for i in 0..n-1:
        for j in i+1..n-1:
            dx = x[i] - x[j], etc.
            d2 = dx²+dy²+dz²
            distance = sqrt(d2)
            mag = dt / (d2 * distance)
            b_i.vx -= dx * mass[j] * mag
            ...
            b_j.vx += dx * mass[i] * mag
            ...
    for each body:
        x += dt * vx, etc.
```

dt = 0.01.

Output format: `printf("%.9f\n", energy)` twice.

